{"task_id": "HumanEval/134", "solution": "def check_if_last_char_is_a_letter(txt):\n    # An empty string cannot satisfy the conditions.\n    if not txt:\n        return False\n\n    last_char = txt[-1]\n\n    # The last character must not be whitespace.\n    if last_char.isspace():\n        return False\n\n    # The last character must be an alphabetical character.\n    if not last_char.isalpha():\n        return False\n\n    # Split the string into words based on spaces.\n    words = txt.split()\n\n    # If there are no words, or if the last word is not valid (e.g., from an empty string input),\n    # this condition might be redundant due to earlier checks, but ensures safety for token retrieval.\n    if not words:\n        return False\n\n    last_token = words[-1]\n\n    # The last token must be a single alphabetical character.\n    return len(last_token) == 1 and last_token.isalpha()"}
